{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-08T14:40:50.944Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1c7226cdcb831e4341d98ac7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-9ke7h9"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"pm contracts has no entry for the files discover subcommand, so its --apply, --note and --append-stable flags are invisible to contract consumers and recovery scanners"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found 2026-11-08 during the CodeRabbit review of PR 1688. pm files discover <id> is an executable Commander subcommand: files discover --help --json lists --append-stable, --apply, --author, --force, --message and --note. The runtime contract surface does not know it. pm contracts --command 'files discover' --flags-only --json refuses with unknown_command, pm contracts --command files lists --migrate but not --apply, and hasSubcommandFlagContractsForCommand returns false for both 'files discover' and 'item files discover'. Consumers that resolve flags from the contracts therefore cannot see the subcommand's options. One example is the read_output_mutation_conflict retry repair from pm-rrwh2o: for 'pm files discover <id> --apply --output-limit 3' it withholds the suggested retry because --apply has no declared arity, although the refusal itself is correct. Expected: files discover (and every other executable subcommand without a contract entry) publishes its flag contracts, so pm contracts, completion and argv-repair scanners resolve them. Duplicate check: searched contracts flags subcommand discover vocabulary missing. pm-ya7x55 and pm-2bqgs7 are closed and covered declared commands and options; pm-6vk110 (open) covers inherited host flags, not missing subcommands."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","contracts","discoverability","files"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-08T14:40:50.944Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-08T14:40:50.944Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"pm contracts --command 'files discover' --flags-only --json lists every flag files discover --help --json reports; a census over the Commander tree fails when an executable subcommand has no contract entry; the read_output_mutation_conflict repair suggests a retry for 'pm files discover <id> --apply --output-limit 3'"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-doxj"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-rrwh2o","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-08T14:40:50.944Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"b45b843f9753b55d329aa48998fc51afc7647c2357a0d64788c2e51b0cc40cbc","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"eb95a133e6e111877a8467db4266e1bcbce25d3c0e2c602e8bec116f9319614c"}
